{
  "skillId": "evaluate-function-algebraic-argument",
  "atomType": "R",
  "theory": {
    "intro": "The input to a function can be an expression, not just a number. $f(x+1)$ means substitute the whole expression $x+1$ for $x$ everywhere in the rule, keeping it in brackets, then expand and simplify. The same idea builds the difference quotient $\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}$.",
    "facts": [
      "$f(x+1)$ means replace every $x$ in the rule with $(x+1)$. For $f(x)=x^2+5x$ this is $(x+1)^2+5(x+1)$.",
      "Expand a squared bracket in full: $(x+1)^2=x^2+2x+1$. The middle term $2x$ is essential — never write $x^2+1$.",
      "Distribute any coefficient over the whole substituted expression, e.g. $5(x+1)=5x+5$.",
      "Watch signs when the argument is negative: $f(-a)$ puts $-a$ in for $x$, so $(-a)^2=a^2$ but $-(-a)=+a$.",
      "For the difference quotient, expand $f(x+h)$, subtract $f(x)$, and simplify the numerator first; every remaining term has a factor of $h$, which then cancels.",
      "Do not cancel the $h$ in the denominator until the numerator has been simplified to a multiple of $h$."
    ],
    "steps": [
      "Substitute the expression for $x$, keeping it in brackets.",
      "Expand squares and distribute coefficients.",
      "Collect like terms to simplify."
    ]
  },
  "practice": {
    "foundation": [
      {
        "question_text": "For $g(x)=2-x$, find $g(a)$.",
        "structure": "sub-linear-argument",
        "solution_text": "$g(a)=2-(a)$\n$=2-a$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $g(x)=2-x$, find $g(a+1)$.",
        "structure": "sub-linear-argument",
        "solution_text": "$g(a+1)=2-(a+1)$\n$=2-a-1$\n$=1-a$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $h(x)=2x+1$, find $h(x+1)$.",
        "structure": "sub-linear-argument",
        "solution_text": "$h(x+1)=2(x+1)+1$\n$=2x+2+1$\n$=2x+3$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=x^2$, find $f(x+1)$.",
        "structure": "sub-square-argument",
        "solution_text": "$f(x+1)=(x+1)^2$\n$=x^2+2x+1$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $h(x)=x^2-2x$, find $h(x+1)$.",
        "structure": "sub-quadratic-argument",
        "solution_text": "$h(x+1)=(x+1)^2-2(x+1)$\n$=x^2+2x+1-2x-2$\n$=x^2-1$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=-x^2$, find $f(x+1)$.",
        "structure": "sub-square-argument",
        "solution_text": "$f(x+1)=-(x+1)^2$\n$=-(x^2+2x+1)$\n$=-x^2-2x-1$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $g(x)=2x+3$, find $g(3-x)$.",
        "structure": "sub-linear-argument",
        "solution_text": "$g(3-x)=2(3-x)+3$\n$=6-2x+3$\n$=9-2x$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=x^2+5x$, find $f(x+1)$.",
        "structure": "sub-quadratic-argument",
        "solution_text": "$f(x+1)=(x+1)^2+5(x+1)$\n$=x^2+2x+1+5x+5$\n$=x^2+7x+6$"
      }
    ],
    "development": [
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=(x-2)(x+6)$, find $f(a+2)$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "sub-quadratic-argument",
        "solution_text": "$f(a+2)=((a+2)-2)((a+2)+6)$\n$=(a)(a+8)$\n$=a^2+8a$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=(x-2)(x+6)$, find $f(a-6)$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "sub-quadratic-argument",
        "solution_text": "$f(a-6)=((a-6)-2)((a-6)+6)$\n$=(a-8)(a)$\n$=a^2-8a$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $g(x)=2-x$, find $g(-a)$.",
        "structure": "sub-negative-argument",
        "solution_text": "$g(-a)=2-(-a)$\n$=2+a$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $F(x)=x^2+2x$, find $F(x-2)$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "sub-quadratic-argument",
        "solution_text": "$F(x-2)=(x-2)^2+2(x-2)$\n$=x^2-4x+4+2x-4$\n$=x^2-2x$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $F(x)=x^2+2x$, find $F(x-h)$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "sub-h-parameter",
        "solution_text": "$F(x-h)=(x-h)^2+2(x-h)$\n$=x^2-2xh+h^2+2x-2h$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=x^2$, find $f(k)-f(k-1)$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "difference-consecutive",
        "solution_text": "$f(k)-f(k-1)=k^2-(k-1)^2$\n$=k^2-(k^2-2k+1)$\n$=k^2-k^2+2k-1$\n$=2k-1$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=3x^2+2x$, find $f(k)-f(k-1)$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "difference-consecutive",
        "solution_text": "$f(k)-f(k-1)=(3k^2+2k)-(3(k-1)^2+2(k-1))$\n$=(3k^2+2k)-(3k^2-4k+1)$\n$=3k^2+2k-3k^2+4k-1$\n$=6k-1$"
      }
    ],
    "mastery": [
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=x^2+5x$, find $\\dfrac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "difference-quotient-point",
        "solution_text": "$f(1+h)=(1+h)^2+5(1+h)$\n$=h^2+7h+6$\n$f(1)=(1)^2+5(1)$\n$=6$\n$\\dfrac{f(1+h)-f(1)}{h}=\\dfrac{(h^2+7h+6)-6}{h}$\n$=\\dfrac{h^2+7h}{h}$\n$=h+7$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=x^2+5x$, find $\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "difference-quotient-general",
        "solution_text": "$f(x+h)=(x+h)^2+5(x+h)$\n$=x^2+2xh+h^2+5x+5h$\n$\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}=\\dfrac{(x^2+2xh+h^2+5x+5h)-(x^2+5x)}{h}$\n$=\\dfrac{2xh+h^2+5h}{h}$\n$=2x+h+5$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $f(x)=2x^2-3x-1$, simplify $\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}$.",
        "structure": "difference-quotient-general",
        "solution_text": "$f(x+h)=2(x+h)^2-3(x+h)-1$\n$=2x^2+4xh+2h^2-3x-3h-1$\n$\\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}=\\dfrac{(2x^2+4xh+2h^2-3x-3h-1)-(2x^2-3x-1)}{h}$\n$=\\dfrac{4xh+2h^2-3h}{h}$\n$=4x+2h-3$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $F(x)=2-x^2$, find $F(t-2)$ in simplest form.",
        "structure": "sub-square-argument",
        "solution_text": "$F(t-2)=2-(t-2)^2$\n$=2-(t^2-4t+4)$\n$=2-t^2+4t-4$\n$=-t^2+4t-2$"
      }
    ]
  }
